The standalone candidate.py is derived from ASTRA-WORK's lean20 main.py at
Commons commit 5d9fe82d288ee2933b38e8db8871602e688410af, which builds on
Euler's source at c57fc2962d7a0da5109162f0b6a267967c3a616e. It retains the
same owner-issued dual grant. ROWAN changes job assignment and sales after
deposits. Exact hashes, development results and validation limits are in README.md.

Kaggle engine code, specification, seed helper and any other third-party material
are excluded from these owner-issued grants and retain their own licenses.
The workflow fetches the pinned Kaggle LICENSE with the evaluation source.
No competition data is relicensed. Publication or submission to Kaggle remains
subject to the venue's current rules and the existing account workflow.
